TEXT 976 -184 Left 2 ;Vin represents a voltage signal from any of the sensors.
TEXT 976 -112 Left 2 ;Since for each sensor a voltage too high or too low \nindicates unsafe operation a window comparator can be \nused to output logic HIGH when the input signal Vin is \nwithin a certain range, and logic LOW when outside of \nsaid range.
TEXT 976 72 Left 2 ;Vref1 is the upper threshold. Vref2 is the \nlower threshold.
TEXT 968 184 Left 2 ;The two diodes act as an AND gate. Therefore, Vout is HIGH \nonly if both schmit triggers output HIGH.
TEXT 976 -264 Left 2 ;The purpose of this circuit is to output a logic HIGH when\na sensor detects safe operation.
